  "worked_solution": "To compute $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}},$ we can use the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\frac{d}{dt}(\\frac{dy}{dx})}{(\\frac{dx}{dt})}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $\\frac{dy}{dx}=-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cot}\u2061(2t),$ and we can calculate $\\frac{dx}{dt}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{dx}{dt}=\\frac{d}{dt}(2\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(2t))=-4\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(2t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\frac{d}{dt}(-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cot}\u2061(2t))}{-4\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(2t)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{csc}^{2}\u2061(2t)}{-4\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(2t)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}{csc}^{3}\u2061(2t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{12},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}{|}_{t=\\pi /12} & =-\\frac{1}{4}{csc}^{3}\u2061(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{12}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4{sin}^{3}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{6})} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{3}} \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
